  "reasoning": "The key 2026 statewide federal benchmark is the U.S. Senate race, where recent Florida polling shows Republican incumbent Ashley Moody narrowly ahead of leading Democratic challenger Angie Nixon by 8 points and ahead of Alex Vindman by 10 points in head\u2011to\u2011head matchups, confirming a Republican advantage at the federal level even as some earlier polling briefly showed a Democrat edging her.[4][13] For statewide context, a July 2026 University of North Florida poll of likely midterm voters in the governor\u2019s race found Republican Byron Donalds leading Democrat David Jolly 46% to 41%, a 5\u2011point GOP margin, while voter registration data from the Florida Division of Elections shows about 5.54 million Republicans vs. 4.03 million Democrats, a record GOP registration edge of roughly 1.5 million voters.[4][8][9][18] Structurally, Florida\u2019s statewide Cook Partisan Voting Index is around R+5, and national and Florida\u2011specific analyses now consistently describe the state as clearly leaning Republican in federal contests rather than a true battleground, so combining the current 5\u20118 point Republican polling leads with the R+5 PVI and large GOP registration edge supports a \"Lean R\" verdict with moderate\u2011high confidence.[1][4][8][9][14][18]",
